      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I disagree with the suggested solution. You should be able to merge nodes regardless of adding new output flows. Having more output flows as a workaround is more complex and should be unnecessary. The flow of execution is not ambiguous, a branch can either go one way, or the other. This is already proven to be possible as other node based scripting languages in Unity already support it without custom output nodes. I have created an example image from Bolt and included it below:",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5e1ba4c4452bd466d14a114e",
      "author": {
        "_id": "596667088f931016208655dc",
        "alias": "Witty Hawk",
        "aliasID": "65ba0158ed6eefce4ceeef69",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/28026ed9e1fcd0b1254c9faf954f8f55.png",
        "created": "2017-07-12T18:14:32.059Z",
        "name": "Ashaka",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": "ashaka"
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5df404cc2072644ac4b5e385",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2020-01-12T22:59:16.514Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
