      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5e0140a6f9212966c1787bc2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I also disagree with this. Having an exit flow just adds more clutter and hurts the simplicity of the branch node.  I could see this being handy in some circumstances, but I think it would make the graph a bit hard to read. It just gives the branch too many responsibilities (evaluate bool, then choose direction, vs evaluate bool, choose direction, and then come back and take a different route).  I know the loop has an exit route, but that needs to be there for the loop to be effective.  Here, not so much.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
